{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgywxkkAW3n68XMpPsW4E","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"1. Nothing is active in my journal, so I'm not sure there is a next step. My best guess is that Bent-Spine, the fence, has more work for me. That's why I went back to ask him, but I never saw a new objective appear. I'd also guess the two clients I turned down might come after me, though the game never said so.\n\n2. Bent-Spine, loosely. Tilts-The-Jug's job was a one-off that S'Tabi pointed me to. Tilts-The-Jug then sent me on to Bent-Spine, who gave me the lockbox job. I do it for coin and because the chain led me there. I don't feel any loyalty, and I don't know what he really wants.\n\n3. The Neeta-Haj sale. The fair-price option needed Speech 30 and I had 15. Option 4 seemed to make her accept in dialogue, but nothing happened in the game. I tried persuade, say 3 and say 4, and couldn't tell whether I'd failed, whether it was bugged, or whether I was missing a step. I ended up giving all three items to her. That wasn't what I wanted, and it meant the other two clients lost out.\n\n4. The setup is good. The dock job and the three lying clients both have a clear moral shape, and the writing is readable. The mechanics let it down in three places:\n   - The strongbox and lockbox were already unlocked, so the lockpicks I was handed never mattered.\n   - A dialogue option that looks like it works but does nothing is the worst kind of failure. Either gate it clearly or make it work.\n   - Tell me when a quest has ended, and what happens to the clients I wronged.\n\n   I'd also like some sign of what comes next, so I'm not left with an empty journal."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3418,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3418},"output_tok